  (text "J1\nWHITE\ntrack" (at 44.0 38.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "J3\nBLACK\ntrack" (at 44.0 58.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "J5\nRED\ntrack" (at 44.0 78.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "J2\nWHITE\nctrl" (at 131.0 38.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "J4\nBLACK\nctrl" (at 131.0 58.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "J6\nRED\nctrl" (at 131.0 78.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "BLACK PATH IS BROKEN HERE BY THE REVERSE SWITCH:\nTrack BLACK (J3) = TRACK_POS. Controller BLACK (J4) = CTRL_BLACK_IN.\nThese are SEPARATE nets — the two N-ch reverse-block switch (sheet 7)\nsits between them. WHITE (J1/J2 = +12V_RAIL) and RED (J5/J6 = GND)\npass straight through; only BLACK is switched." (at 45.0 95.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2) bold)))
  (text "Module inserts between track and controller.\nDuring normal forward drive the switch is fully on (low Rds),\nso the module is near-transparent on BLACK (~27-47mV at 40A).\nBrake detection: voltage sense on BLACK, tapped on the TRACK side\n(TRACK_POS) of the switch -> PA1." (at 45.0 112.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "SIGNAL DESCRIPTIONS:\nWHITE (+12-16V):  Always-live rail from track PSU (40-90A). Powers module\n                  via F1+LDO. Also feeds the ideal-diode gate-drive charge pump and the anti-brake current source.\nBLACK (track +):  Controlled by hand controller (0 to rail voltage).\n                  Falls to near 0V when controller shorts for braking.\nRED (common -):   Braid return. Common ground reference (GND)." (at 45.0 130.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "BRAKE DETECTION (this module):\nV_BLACK < 500mV  => enter brake state\nV_BLACK > 1500mV => exit brake state\nHysteresis prevents chatter at low throttle." (at 45.0 152.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
)
